# Line endings for files a tool writes and a tool then checks.
#
# This exists because of one CI failure that could not happen locally. The
# generated API types are written by openapi-typescript with LF endings;
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default and checks text files out as
# CRLF; and `npm run api:types:check` compares the file on disk against what
# the generator would write. So a freshly checked-out tree disagreed with the
# generator about 4,021 carriage returns, and the drift gate reported drift
# that did not exist.
#
# It passed on the machine that wrote the file -- because that file had never
# been through a checkout -- and failed for everybody else, which is the worst
# shape a check can have.
#
# Pinning the generated file to LF makes the two agree. Scoped to the files
# that are machine-written and machine-compared rather than applied to the
# whole tree: normalising everything else would rewrite every file in the repo
# for no reason anybody asked for.
ui/src/api-types.gen.ts text eol=lf

# The OpenAPI snapshot is the other half of the same pair: written by
# tools/openapi_snapshot.py and compared byte-for-byte by a test.
backend/tests/openapi.json text eol=lf
